<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles University</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1348</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as University of Prague</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles University in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> was founded by Charles IV in 1348, the first university in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-europe">Central Europe</a>. In the early fifteenth century it was a centre of the Hussite movement, and the Decree of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kutna-hora">Kutná Hora</a> of 1409 gave the Czech nation control, prompting German masters to leave. In 1882 it was divided into Czech and German universities; the German one was closed in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-university.jpg" alt="Charles University" width="320" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: WikiWriter123 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charles-University-symbol-4.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
